{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Old and satisfied</b> — that he saw every desire of his heart and was satisfied with every good thing. Similarly, \"satisfied with days\" (Genesis 35:29) — his soul was satisfied with the days and he did not crave that the days renew anything in him. This is like what is said of David: \"And he died at a good old age, satisfied with days, riches, and honor\" (I Chronicles 29:28). This is a recounting of the kindnesses of HaShem toward the righteous and the good measure He gives them, that they do not crave surpluses, as it is said of them: \"The desire of his heart You have given him\" (Psalms 21:3) — and not as is said of the rest of men: \"He who loves silver will not be satisfied with silver\" (Ecclesiastes 5:9). And they said about this (Ecclesiastes Rabbah 1:13): No man departs from the world with even half his desire in his hand — he has one hundred, he craves two hundred; he reaches two hundred, he craves four hundred, as it is said: \"He who loves silver will not be satisfied with silver\" (Genesis Rabbah 62:1). They said: The Holy One, blessed be He, shows the righteous the reward that He is destined to give them in the World to Come, and their soul is satisfied and they sleep. The Sages were awakened by this and explained the verse that says \"and satisfied\" as referring to this vision:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'and they sleep' (והם ישנים) likely refers to the righteous dying in peace after being shown their reward; the translation is rendered hyper-literally to preserve the concise midrastic idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:34.885280046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}